1
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,560
Thanks for coming by.
謝謝你們趕過來

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,890
We wanted to bounce some ideas off of you about the wedding ceremony.
我們希望你們能幫我們 想一些婚禮上用的點子

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,770
-What's the matter? Are you okay? -It's just...
-怎麼了？你還好嗎？ -那只是因為…

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,570
Monica said "wedding."
摩妮卡說了「婚禮」

5
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:18,440
We thought one of you could read something.
我們希望你們之中 有人能上台念些感性的文章

6
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:22,270
Okay, yeah, I guess I can do that too.
好吧，我想我應該也能勝任

7
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,210
Too?
也能勝任？

8
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:29,290
I kind of have something else planned for you guys.
我自己想了一個點子 來慶祝你們的婚禮

9
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:32,220
-Do you mind telling us what it is? -Sorry.
-你能告訴我們是什麼點子嗎？ -抱歉

10
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:35,760
I'm kind of keeping this one on the QT.
我想把它當成是高度機密

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,630
Whatever it is, I hope it involves winking.
不管你是指哪個，我希望會有眨眼睛

12
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:42,400
-Hey. -Hey.
-嘿 -嘿

13
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:44,730
I talked to one of the DOOL writers..
我跟DOOL的編劇談過…

14
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:47,170
-What is DOOL? -Days Of Our Lives.
-什麼是DOOL？ -《我們的日子》

15
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:53,010
You won't believe it. My character is coming out of his coma!
你們一定不相信 我演的角色就要醒過來了

16
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,150
-That's wonderful. -Wow, Joey.
-那真的是太棒了 -哇，喬伊

17
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:59,110
And not only that. I'm getting a new brain!
不只是那個，我會有個新腦子！

18
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:04,320
So great things are happening at work and in your personal life.
你的工作跟私生活 都有了很棒的進展

19
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:07,090
You're getting a new brain?
你要換個新腦子？

20
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,990
They're killing off one of the characters...
他們要踢走劇中一個角色…

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:13,170
and her brain is being transplanted into my body.
將她的腦子移植到我的身體裡

22
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:18,510
What? A brain transplant?
什麼？腦部移植手術？

23
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:20,330
It's ridiculous.
這太可笑了

24
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:23,770
It's ridiculous that you haven't had sex in three months.
可笑的是你三個半月沒有做過愛

25
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:32,280
It's winter. There are fewer people on the street.
現在是冬天，街上的人少了很多

26
00:01:33,690 --> 00:01:34,920
Who are they killing off?
他們要踢走誰？

27
00:01:35,190 --> 00:01:37,680
Cecilia Monroe. She plays Jessica Lockhart.
西西雅夢露，她飾演潔西卡拉哈特

28
00:01:37,930 --> 00:01:39,390
No!
不！

29
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,690
She is so good at throwing drinks in people's faces.
她最擅長將飲料潑到別人臉上

30
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:46,590
I don't think I've ever seen her finish a drink.
我從來沒看過她喝完一杯飲料

31
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:49,390
The way she slaps people. Wouldn't you love to?
還有她打人巴掌的樣子 你不想那麼做嗎？

32
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:51,160
Don't do it.
別那麼做

33
00:01:52,010 --> 00:01:53,870
And she's been on the show forever.
她參與這齣戲的演出很久了

34
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:56,670
It's gonna be really hard to fill her shoes.
要代替她一定很難

35
00:01:56,850 --> 00:01:58,040
Help me out here.
你得幫幫我

36
00:01:58,310 --> 00:02:02,810
When you come out of the brain transplant...
當你做過腦部移植手術後…

37
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:05,920
you are going to be her?
你要變成她？

38
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:09,060
Yes, but in Drake Ramoray's body.
對，她被困在德瑞克的身體裡

39
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:15,590
Why is this so hard for you to get? I thought you were a scientist.
你為什麼就是搞不懂？ 我還以為你是科學家

40
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:19,260
The One Where Joey Gets A New Brain
本集播出：喬伊的新腦袋

00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:21,260
rainystar壓制iPod-MP4

41
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,000
Rach, so that guy there:
瑞秋，那邊那個男的…

42
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,330
Straight or gay?
是異性戀還是同性戀？

43
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:04,340
Oh, yeah, he's too cute to be straight.
他太帥了，不可能是異性戀

44
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:07,710
Knockers will help us figure it out.
大波霸小姐會幫我們查個清楚

45
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:15,150
All right, straight.
好了，他是異性戀

46
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,720
And not subtle.
而且一眼就看得出來

47
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:21,760
He left his cell phone.
他忘了拿手機

48
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:24,760
We could have Gunther put it in lost and found.
我們得把它交給阿甘 放在失物招領處

49
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:28,660
Or we could use it to call China, see how those guys are doing.
或是用它打電話到中國 看看那些人在做什麼

50
00:03:29,370 --> 00:03:32,530
What if he calls his own cell phone and I answer...
如果他打電話來找手機 我接了電話…

51
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:36,170
and we start talking and we fell in love?
我們開始聊天，之後墜入愛河呢？

52
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:38,540
Would that be a great story?
那是個很棒的故事吧？

53
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:41,610
Kind of like a fairy tale for the digital age.
就像是數位時代的童話故事

54
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:44,510
That does sound great. I'm getting the phone.
那聽起來很棒，我要去拿手機

55
00:03:44,790 --> 00:03:48,050
What? Wait. Why do you get the story?
什麼？等一下 為什麼你會成為故事的女主角？

56
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:50,990
I haven't been out on a date in so long.
我已經很久沒有約會了

57
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:53,690
Phoebe, you had a date three days ago.
菲比，三天前你才約過會

58
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:58,520
That wasn't a date. That was friends getting together and having sex.
那不是約會，那只是 朋友聚會，然後做愛

59
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,890
Okay. Great. I get the phone.
好吧，我去拿手機

60
00:04:01,170 --> 00:04:04,300
No way. You just broke up with Tag a week ago.
不行，一星期前你才跟泰格分手

61
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:09,810
Yeah, and until now, I didn't think I would love again.
對，直到現在，我才明白 我能再愛一次

62
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:12,070
-Nice try. -Wait.
-說的好 -等一下

63
00:04:12,350 --> 00:04:15,410
How do we fairly decide who gets the phone?
我們該怎麼公平地決定 誰能拿走手機呢？

64
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,480
I don't know.
我不知道

65
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,860
Maybe we could...
或許我們可以…

66
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,230
Ah-ha! Too slow!
你動作太慢了！

67
00:04:31,530 --> 00:04:34,230
Ah-ha! Too cocky.
你太自大了

68
00:04:36,643 --> 00:04:38,167
（銀杯片廠）

69
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:41,010
I'm dating him. There's nothing you can do.
我在跟他約會，你管不了

70
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:42,230
Yes, there is.
不，我管得了

71
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:45,740
Are you going to kill him like you did Charles?
你打算怎麼做？殺了他嗎？ 就像你殺了查爾斯？

72
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:50,450
Oh, my baby.
我的寶貝

73
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:56,290
Cut!
卡！

74
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:05,060
That was great. And that slap looked so real. How do you do that?
你演得太好了，剛剛那一巴掌 很逼真，你怎麼辦到的？

75
00:05:05,270 --> 00:05:08,930
-Oh, just years of experience. -Can I get some ice here?!
-那只是多年的經驗 -快拿冰塊過來給我

76
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,440
I just wanted to say how wonderful I think you are.
我只想說我覺得你的演技很棒

77
00:05:13,810 --> 00:05:16,300
You're not the fan who's dying,  are you?
你該不會是那個快死掉的影迷吧？

78
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,500
I'm Joey Tribbiani. We did a scene together yesterday.
我是喬伊崔比亞尼 昨天我們合拍過一場戲

79
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:24,120
-I'm the guy in the coma. -Oh, that was a real person?
-我就是那個昏迷的人 -那是真人？

80
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:30,520
Since I'm getting your brain when you leave the show...
因為你離開後我要移植你的腦子…

81
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,620
I was wondering if..
我在想如果…

82
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:36,350
-I'm leaving the show? -Why? Did you hear something?
-我要離開？ -為什麼？你聽到了什麼？

83
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,230
Who told you that?
是誰告訴你的？

84
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:44,000
-One of the writers. -Was it bald or was it tall?
-編劇之一 -哪個編劇？是禿頭佬還是高個子？

85
00:05:45,010 --> 00:05:48,130
You know, it doesn't matter,  because it is not true.
那不重要，因為那不是真的

86
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:49,570
Okay.
好吧

87
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:53,370
And if it were true, how dare you come to me and ask me for tips...
如果那是真的 你竟然敢來叫我教你…

88
00:05:53,610 --> 00:05:56,310
about a character I've played for 20 years!
該如何飾演我演了二十年的角色

89
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,320
Miss Monroe.. Oh, there you go.
夢露小姐…喔，你真的那麼做了

90
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:10,060
Okay, look, I have an idea.
好吧，聽著，我有個點子

91
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:14,630
Why don't we see what kind of numbers he has on his speed dial...
我們為什麼不看看 他的速撥鍵記錄了哪些電話號碼…

92
00:06:14,870 --> 00:06:19,360
and then whoever has more in common with him gets the phone.
跟他有最多共通點的人 就可以把手機拿走

93
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,840
-Fine. All right. -All right.
-好吧 -好吧

94
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:26,340
First name on the speed dial is "Mom."
速撥鍵的第一個名字是「媽媽」

95
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:29,380
Oh. I lost my mom to suicide.
喔，我媽媽自殺死了

96
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:33,480
You can't use that to get the cute guy and the last blueberry muffin.
不行，你不能利用那一點 搶走帥哥跟最後一塊藍莓鬆餅

97
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:36,280
Did I use that already today? Sorry.
今天我已經用過那個借口了？對不起

98
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:41,160
"Ben, Carlos, David.."
班，卡洛斯，大衛…

99
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:44,830
Oh, I win. He's got Barney's on his speed dial.
我贏了，他在速撥鍵裡記下了巴尼斯

100
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:47,500
You don't know it's Barney's the store.
你不知道他指的是不是巴尼斯服飾店

101
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:50,330
That could be his friend's house, a bar..
那可能是他朋友家或是酒吧的電話…

102
00:06:50,570 --> 00:06:52,730
Who has Barney's the store on their speed dial?
誰會把巴尼斯服飾店的電話 記錄成速撥鍵？

103
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:55,070
His new girlfriend.
他的新女朋友

104
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,320
What is that?
那是什麼聲音？

105
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:13,350
I think it's the Dying Cat Parade.
我想是快死掉的貓在舉行遊行

106
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,190
Sounds like it's coming from across the street.
聽起來是從對街傳來的

107
00:07:18,670 --> 00:07:21,930
-Oh, my God. -What?
-我的天啊 -什麼？

108
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:24,500
The thing that Ross was gonna do at our wedding?
還記得羅斯說他要在 婚禮上給我們驚喜嗎？

109
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:28,440
He was hanging out with me and said,  "You're half Scottish, right?"
他跟我出去混時說： 「你有蘇格蘭的血統吧？」

110
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:32,370
No. There is no way. It cannot be Ross.
不，不可能，不可能是羅斯

111
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:44,050
Unbelievable. Why is your family Scottish?
不可思議，為什麼你有蘇格蘭血統？

112
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:48,190
Why is your family Ross?
為什麼羅斯是你哥哥？

113
00:07:49,730 --> 00:07:52,360
He cannot play at our wedding.
他不能在婚禮上演奏 大家都會跑光的

114
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:55,760
I mean, come on. That is just noise!
我是說那只是噪音！

115
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,900
It's not even a song.
那根本不算是歌

116
00:07:58,970 --> 00:08:01,500
Wait. If you listen very carefully...
等一下，如果你仔細聽…

117
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:04,740
I think it's "Celebration" by Kool and the Gang.
我想它是庫爾 與夥伴合唱團唱的《慶祝》

118
00:08:10,850 --> 00:08:13,840
You're right. They are writing me out of the show.
你說的對，他們要將我踢出這齣戲

119
00:08:14,090 --> 00:08:17,490
They don't know exactly when it's going to happen, but soon...
他們還沒有決定 什麼時候，但應該很快…

120
00:08:17,730 --> 00:08:19,280
and then that's it.
就是這樣了

121
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:22,550
If it was up to me,  you would never leave the show.
我真的很抱歉，如果我可以決定 你永遠都不會離開這齣戲

122
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,890
-Yeah, thanks. -I mean it.
-謝謝你 -我是認真的

123
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:28,400
I can't believe they'd do this to you. And to your fans.
我不敢相信他們會對你這麼做 還有你的影迷

124
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:33,010
They're gonna be devastated. Heartbroken. They love you so much.
他們一定會崩潰傷心 他們是那麼地愛你

125
00:08:33,610 --> 00:08:35,510
Oh, you're right.
你說的對

126
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,410
Thank you.
謝謝

127
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:39,440
What's your name again?
你說你叫什麼名字？

128
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:42,280
-Joey. -Thank you.
-喬伊 -謝謝你

129
00:08:42,550 --> 00:08:44,710
That is so sweet.
那真的太貼心了

130
00:08:45,390 --> 00:08:47,950
The only reason I came up to you before...
聽著，之前我會來找你...

131
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:49,810
is because, well...
是因為…

132
00:08:50,090 --> 00:08:53,120
I'm really nervous about being you.
因為要飾演你我真的很緊張

133
00:08:53,330 --> 00:08:57,390
If you could help me capture the essence of the character...
請你幫我抓住角色的精髓

134
00:08:57,630 --> 00:09:00,260
Help me keep Jessica alive. Please?
幫助我讓潔西卡 繼續活下去，可以嗎？

135
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:04,200
Joey, I will help you.
好吧，喬伊，我會幫你

136
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:07,910
Not because I owe it to this stupid show...
不是因為我對這出蠢戲有虧欠…

137
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:11,340
but because I owe it to Jessica.
而是因為我虧欠潔西卡

138
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:14,340
-Oh, thank you so much. -You're so welcome.
-那真的是太棒了，謝謝你 -別客氣

139
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:17,240
I've been watching some tapes. How's this?
我一直在觀摩錄影帶 你覺得這招如何？

140
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:21,640
Jessica Lockhart will never step foot in this place again!
潔西卡拉哈特 永遠都不會再踏入這裡！

141
00:09:21,890 --> 00:09:23,080
Never!
永遠都不會！

142
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:29,190
Jessica doesn't have an English accent.
但潔西卡沒有英國腔

143
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:31,520
I can do an English accent?
我有英國腔？

144
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:36,330
That baby's going on my resume.
我要把這點寫在我的履歷表裡

145
00:09:40,110 --> 00:09:42,410
-Hi. How are you? -Good.
-嗨，你好嗎？ -我很好

146
00:09:42,610 --> 00:09:45,080
Remember when we were in the coffeehouse...
還記得我們在咖啡廳時…

147
00:09:45,350 --> 00:09:48,370
we decided I was gonna keep the cute guy's phone?
我們決定我可以 拿走那個帥哥的手機嗎？

148
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:53,180
I was gonna keep it in my purse, so if it rang, I could just pick it up?
我要把它放在我的皮包裡 如果它響了，我就能立刻接聽？

149
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:58,620
Do you remember going into my purse and stealing the phone?
你還記得你從我的皮包 把手機偷走了嗎？

150
00:10:00,090 --> 00:10:01,430
Ooh, now you lost me.
我聽不懂你在說什麼

151
00:10:01,930 --> 00:10:04,020
-You stole the phone. -No, I didn't.
-你偷走了手機 -不，我沒有

152
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:07,260
You're saying if I called it,  it wouldn't ring?
如果我撥號過去它不會響嗎？

153
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:08,590
-No. -Okay.
-不會 -好吧

154
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:13,400
But while you dial, let me show you the features of my new ringing handbag.
既然你要撥號了，我要讓你看看 我剛買的響鈴皮包

155
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:17,130
Oh, it does work.
喔，它真的有用

156
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:20,510
-Phoebe. -That is a different phone.
-菲比 -那是另一隻手機

157
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:25,520
Oh, is it? Hello. Yes, hi. Is Rachel there?
是嗎？喂，對，你好，瑞秋在嗎？

158
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:29,120
Yes, she is. Just one moment, please. It's for me!
她在，請稍等，是找我的！

159
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,920
That is damning evidence.
那是鐵證

160
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:38,020
Oh, my God. I bet that's him.
我的天啊，我敢說是他打來的

161
00:10:38,430 --> 00:10:40,590
My digital fairy tale's about to begin.
我的數位童話故事就要開始了

162
00:10:43,170 --> 00:10:45,570
Would you stop doing that?
你能不能別再那麼做了？

163
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:48,670
Hello? Yes, I'm the one who found your phone.
喂，對，我就是撿到你手機的人

164
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,470
-Phoebe, you can't.. -Shh, I'm on a call.
-菲比，你不能… -我在講電話

165
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:57,650
Yeah, you can pick it up tonight. Say,8:30?
對，今晚你能過來拿，就八點半吧？

166
00:10:57,920 --> 00:11:00,750
At my apartment.
到我家來

167
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:04,480
It's 5 Morton Street, apartment 14.
摩頓街五號，十四號房

168
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:08,860
And then maybe, you know, after, we can grab a bite to eat or whatever.
或許之後我們可以去吃點東西

169
00:11:09,130 --> 00:11:11,430
Okay. Okay, I'll see you then. Bye.
好的，到時候見，再見

170
00:11:13,930 --> 00:11:16,560
I will be here when he comes over.
你知道他來的時候我會在這裡

171
00:11:16,770 --> 00:11:18,930
How will you know what time to come over?
你怎麼知道他什麼時候會來？

172
00:11:19,210 --> 00:11:21,470
You just said it.
你剛剛說出來了

173
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:25,770
Oh.

174
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:34,780
The essence of the character is rooted in her confidence.
這個角色的精髓源自於她的自信

175
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:37,790
So when Jessica enters a room, for instance...
譬如說，當潔西卡走進一個房間時…

176
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,960
she owns everything...
她擁有那個房間裡…

177
00:11:40,230 --> 00:11:43,890
and every person in that room.
所有事物跟所有人

178
00:11:45,430 --> 00:11:47,230
-You try it. -Okay.
-你來試試看 -好吧

179
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:57,570
He's not mad at the room.
他沒有對這個房間生氣

180
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:01,910
Try it again. He owns it. He owns the room.
再試一次，他擁有它 他擁有這個房間

181
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:06,810
It is his. He owns, owns, owns the room! He owns it!
這是他的，他擁有 這個房間！他擁有它！

182
00:12:07,490 --> 00:12:09,720
It's a little weird, but it's getting better.
這有點奇怪，但已經好多了

183
00:12:11,830 --> 00:12:15,990
I'm gonna miss this woman so much. I don't know what I'm gonna do.
我一定會很想念這個女人 我不知道我該怎麼辦

184
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:18,490
It's been 20 years of my life.
我演這齣戲二十年了

185
00:12:18,970 --> 00:12:22,460
Hey, hey. Maybe this is a good thing.
或許這是件好事

186
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:26,700
It'll give you a chance to shake things up. Play different characters.
它給你機會做改變 扮演不一樣的角色

187
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:28,310
You're so talented.
你才華洋溢

188
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:33,280
Probably should've just left years ago when the offers were pouring in...
或許我該在幾年前離開 那時很多人要我接戲…

189
00:12:33,510 --> 00:12:36,480
but I just got so comfy here and...
但我在這裡過得太舒服…

190
00:12:36,780 --> 00:12:39,150
I turned down some amazing work.
我拒絕了一些大好機會

191
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:40,750
Like what?
譬如說呢？

192
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:44,520
Well, let's just say if I'd left 15 years ago...
喔，就說如果我在十五年前離開…

193
00:12:44,790 --> 00:12:49,320
the landscape of Mexican cinema would be very different today.
現在的墨西哥影壇會完全不一樣

194
00:12:51,330 --> 00:12:53,030
Wow.
哇

195
00:12:54,470 --> 00:12:59,500
But, well, now... Now's a different time for me.
但現在…現在時機不一樣了

196
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:05,340
Oh, hey, come on. Don't do this.
嘿，別這樣

197
00:13:05,610 --> 00:13:07,840
Let me tell you something, okay?
聽我說句話，好嗎？

198
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:12,780
When I watch you do a scene, I'm thinking, "She is a great actress."
當我看到你演戲時 我想「天啊，她是個很棒的演員」

199
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:17,650
But I'm also thinking, "She is hot."
但我也會想「她好辣」

200
00:13:19,860 --> 00:13:21,950
You think I'm hot?
你覺得我很辣？

201
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:25,060
You own the room.
你擁有這個房間

202
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:31,640
We should probably get the...
或許我們應該…

203
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:34,030
Oh, yeah. Yeah, we should get..
對，我們應該…

204
00:13:38,350 --> 00:13:42,370
So when Jessica kisses a man...
當潔西卡吻男人時…

205
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:46,050
she usually puts...
她通常會把…

206
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:49,190
both her hands on the man's face.
雙手放在那個男人臉上

207
00:13:49,420 --> 00:13:51,890
I notice that. Is that because she's so passionate?
我注意到了，那是因為她 充滿了熱情嗎？

208
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:55,530
No, it's because that way the camera only sees her.
不，那是因為 那樣子攝影機只能拍到她

209
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,370
You want to try it?
你想試試看嗎？

210
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:03,660
Yeah, okay.
好的

211
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:18,440
That was good. That was really good.
太棒了，真的很不錯

212
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:25,560
But I think that maybe your hands are just a little off. They should..
但我想你手的位置不對 它們應該…

213
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,960
Well, I feel like a snack.
我想吃點點心

214
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:40,870
Do you want some shortbread? It's Scottish, like you are.
你要吃點脆餅嗎？ 它是你故鄉蘇格蘭的點心

215
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:45,470
Oh, no, thanks. I don't like anything from my Scottish heritage.
不，謝謝，我不喜歡蘇格蘭的東西

216
00:14:45,750 --> 00:14:47,240
What?
什麼？

217
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:51,910
Well, it's just that my entire family was run out of Scotland by...
因為我的家族被趕出蘇格蘭…

218
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,640
Vikings.
是維京人幹的

219
00:14:55,560 --> 00:15:00,360
It sounds like your family's ready to rediscover its Scottish roots.
聽起來你家人 準備要恢復蘇格蘭傳統

220
00:15:00,590 --> 00:15:02,060
You can't play bagpipes at the wedding!
你不能在婚禮上吹風笛！

221
00:15:04,430 --> 00:15:05,760
How did you know?
你們怎麼知道？

222
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:10,900
-We heard you play from our apartment. -Were you the ones who called the cops?
-我們聽到你在家裡吹風笛 -是你們去報警的？

223
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:14,500
That's not really important right now.
現在那真的不重要

224
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:18,270
What is important is, while we appreciate the gesture...
重要的是，我們謝謝你的好意…

225
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:22,640
we just don't feel that bagpipes are appropriate for our wedding.
我們只是覺得 我們的婚禮上不適合吹風笛

226
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:26,010
-Why not? -Because we hate them.
-為什麼？ -因為我們討厭風笛

227
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:30,390
Just give me a chance to perform for you, then decide whatever you want.
給我機會為你們表演 再做最後的決定

228
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:34,080
I'm not gonna tell you what song I'm gonna play, either.
我也不會告訴你們 我要吹哪首曲子

229
00:15:34,330 --> 00:15:36,160
Let's just say when it's over...
就說當表演結束後…

230
00:15:36,430 --> 00:15:40,300
I'll bet there'll be a wee bit o'celebration.
我們一定會慶祝一下

231
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:49,200
Hey, hey!
嘿！

232
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:52,540
Who is it?
是誰？

233
00:15:53,210 --> 00:15:55,480
It's Tom. I'm here to pick up the phone.
我是湯姆，我來拿手機的

234
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:59,790
Why do you get to answer the door?
為什麼要由你去開門？

235
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:02,610
-Why shouldn't I? -Because it's my apartment.
-為什麼不行？ -因為這裡是我家

236
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:04,920
Then I get to give him the phone.
那麼由我來把手機交給他

237
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:08,620
Okay. Good luck explaining all the calls to China.
好吧，希望你能好好 跟他解釋那些打到中國的電話

238
00:16:11,530 --> 00:16:12,790
Hi.
嗨

239
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,300
Wow, how long were we arguing for?
我們爭執了多久？

240
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,970
You're not the man who left the phone.
你不是那個忘了拿手機的人

241
00:16:26,210 --> 00:16:29,510
-No, that's my assistant. -Is he coming?
-對，他是我的助理 -他會來嗎？

242
00:16:30,450 --> 00:16:31,710
No.
不會

243
00:16:31,990 --> 00:16:34,750
-Could you give us one second? -Sure.
-你能讓我們談一下嗎？ -沒問題

244
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:37,220
We'll be right back, sir.
我們馬上回來

245
00:16:38,690 --> 00:16:42,030
-What do we do? -I don't know.
-我們該怎麼辦？ -我不知道

246
00:16:42,330 --> 00:16:43,690
Can you believe this?
你能相信嗎？

247
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:47,090
We were waiting for a hot guy and a hotter one shows up.
我們在等一個帥哥 結果來了一個超級大帥哥

248
00:16:47,370 --> 00:16:48,700
I know..
我知道

249
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:54,170
What?
什麼？

250
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:55,400
Rachel, listen...
瑞秋，聽我說…

251
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:59,700
if you let me have him, then I will really owe you one.
如果你能把他讓給我 我真的欠你一個大人情

252
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,420
All right.
好吧

253
00:17:05,290 --> 00:17:07,580
All right, I will let you have him.
好吧，我把他讓給你

254
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,910
But you owe me. You owe me big.
但你欠我一個大人情

255
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:13,580
Which one of you will I take to dinner?
哪一位漂亮的小姐要陪我去吃晚餐？

256
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:16,020
Oh, that'd be me, sir.
是我

257
00:17:16,969 --> 00:17:19,665
-你先請 -謝謝

258
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:22,030
Nice.
太棒了

259
00:17:27,710 --> 00:17:31,080
Well, you certainly own that room.
你的確擁有那個房間

260
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:37,220
Actually, I rent the whole place. I just got what you meant. Thank you.
事實上我租下整間公寓 我剛瞭解你的意思，謝謝誇獎

261
00:17:40,620 --> 00:17:41,820
-Hi. -Hey.
-嗨 -嘿

262
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:44,920
Oh, my God.
我的天啊

263
00:17:45,530 --> 00:17:47,020
Oh, my God.
我的天啊

264
00:17:47,730 --> 00:17:51,560
Oh, Jessica Lockhart! In my apartment!
潔西卡拉哈特！在我家裡面！

265
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:55,000
I am such a huge fan. I am such a huge fan.
我是你的頭號大影迷 我是你的頭號大影迷

266
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,500
It's nice to know..
很高興能知道…

267
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:58,140
Monica!
摩妮卡！

268
00:18:00,010 --> 00:18:02,240
That's my roommate, Rachel.
她是我的室友瑞秋

269
00:18:02,510 --> 00:18:04,480
That explains the women's underwear.
難怪你家會有女人內衣

270
00:18:04,710 --> 00:18:06,300
Sure.
沒錯

271
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:10,180
Oh, my God, it's true!
我的天啊，是真的！

272
00:18:12,650 --> 00:18:15,750
Can I just ask you to do me just one favor?
我的天啊，我能請你幫我一個忙嗎？

273
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:17,460
Certainly.
當然可以

275
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:20,490
Would you slap me right here in the face?
你能打我一巴掌嗎？

276
00:18:22,230 --> 00:18:26,170
I'd love to, but my lawyer said I can't do that anymore.
我很願意，但我的律師說 我不能再那麼做了

277
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,760
All right, here we go.
好了，我們走吧

278
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,100
No, wait. Just one moment.
不，等一下，還有一件事

279
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:37,340
-You're a stupid bitch. -I really can't slap you.
-你是個笨女人 -我真的不能打你巴掌

280
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:41,500
-My God, you're great. -Thanks for stopping by.
-我的天啊，你太棒了 -謝謝你們過來

281
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:45,680
-I am so sorry about that. -Oh, no.
-我真的很抱歉 -不

282
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:48,750
Being adored, I'm used to it. Don't worry about it.
我習慣被影迷包圍，別擔心

283
00:18:49,990 --> 00:18:51,480
-Oh, my God. -What?
-我的天啊 -什麼？

284
00:18:51,860 --> 00:18:54,620
They sent me today's script. They never send me the script.
他們寄了今天的劇本來給我 他們從來沒有寄劇本給過我

285
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:57,060
-They don't? -I'm in a coma.
-是嗎？ -我一直都昏迷不醒

286
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:59,770
This must mean I have lines.
這代表我有台詞了

287
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,700
Oh.

288
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:05,800
How does it happen?
我是怎麼死的？

289
00:19:09,810 --> 00:19:13,540
You get thrown from a horse into an electric fence.
你摔下馬，然後撞到電籬笆

290
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:17,610
A what? Jessica hates horses.
什麼？潔西卡討厭馬

291
00:19:17,890 --> 00:19:21,880
After this she's not gonna be crazy about electricity, either.
經過這件事，她也不會喜歡電

292
00:19:26,730 --> 00:19:30,320
Loosening the saddle on Mother's horse was brilliant, Fredrick.
在媽媽的馬鞍上動手腳 是個超級好點子，佛萊德克

293
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:33,160
And the electric fence, inspired.
電籬笆那個點子太妙了

294
00:19:33,430 --> 00:19:34,800
Thank you, sweetheart.
謝謝你，親愛的

295
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:38,270
I can't believe she's really gone.
我不敢相信她真的死了

296
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,400
Look around you. All of this is ours.
看看你的四周，一切都是你的

297
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,340
I don't think so.
我可不那麼認為

298
00:19:48,750 --> 00:19:49,810
Who are you?
你是誰？

299
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,910
What's the matter, Dina?
怎麼了？笛娜

300
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:54,820
Don't you recognize your own...
你不認得你自己的…

301
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:56,490
mother?
媽媽嗎？

302
00:19:59,430 --> 00:20:02,120
Cut! That was great, everybody. Thank you.
卡！大家都演得很好，謝謝

303
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:04,830
That was so wonderful!
那真的是太棒了

304
00:20:05,070 --> 00:20:08,360
I think that you're a better Jessica than I ever was.
我想你比我更適合演潔西卡

305
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:11,430
-Oh, no. -Of course not, but you were good.
-喔，不 -當然不是，但你真的很棒

306
00:20:11,670 --> 00:20:12,800
Thanks.
謝謝

307
00:20:13,070 --> 00:20:15,200
Good news. I got another job.
好消息，我找到新工作了

308
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,840
Great. Hey, all right! What is it?
太棒了，是什麼樣的工作

309
00:20:18,110 --> 00:20:20,270
A film in Guadalajara.
我要到瓜達拉哈拉拍電影

310
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:22,970
The airport?
你是指那個機場？

311
00:20:25,150 --> 00:20:26,590
No, that's LaGuardia.
不，那是拉瓜迪亞機場

312
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:33,660
-This is Mexico. -Oh, wow.
-我要去墨西哥 -哇

313
00:20:33,890 --> 00:20:36,160
Well, how long will you be gone?
你會去多久？

314
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,190
Eight months.
八個月

315
00:20:39,130 --> 00:20:42,800
-That's a really long time. -Yeah, but you could come and visit.
-那真的很久 -對，但你可以來看我

316
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:47,240
I bet you could own a few places down there.
我敢說你能在那裡擁有幾個地方

317
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:52,170
Oh, you know, I should probably buy a place in the city first.
你知道的，或許我該先在紐約買房子

318
00:20:54,210 --> 00:20:56,740
And I just got what you meant. That is..
我剛瞭解你的意思，那…

319
00:20:57,020 --> 00:20:59,250
-That's a tricky one. -It's tricky.
-那真的有難度 -真的很難

320
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,420
Good luck.
祝你好運

321
00:21:05,330 --> 00:21:06,880
You too.
你也是

322
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:26,770
Now, remember, I'm still learning.
請記住 我還在學吹風笛

324
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:38,980
One, two, three, four!
一，二，三，四！

325
